# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability suppression list
#
# Add CVE IDs here to suppress false positives or accepted risks.
# One CVE per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Run the pipeline — if it fails on a CRITICAL CVE, note the CVE ID
#      from the Trivy output (e.g. CVE-2023-XXXXX).
#   2. Research the CVE at https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/search to confirm
#      whether it actually affects your usage.
#   3. If it is a false positive or not exploitable in your setup,
#      add the CVE ID below with a comment explaining why it is safe to ignore.
#   4. Commit this file — the suppression applies on every future scan.
#
# FORMAT:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # short reason why this is suppressed
#
# EXAMPLE (do not uncomment unless you have verified these apply):
#   CVE-2023-44487  # HTTP/2 Rapid Reset — mitigated by ALB in front of the app
#   CVE-2023-46589  # Tomcat partial PUT — feature disabled in our config
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Add verified suppressions below this line
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
